  "residual_risks": [
    "Default character estimates cover the declared serialized payload, not a real tokenizer upper bound, pricing or provider-internal additions",
    "Generic Model profiles cannot see hidden third-party provider wrapping; declared model windows/overheads are not live service measurements",
    "Three bounded preparations may conservatively reject an otherwise packable history; added JSON copies have CPU/memory overhead",
    "Cumulative actual-token accounting, transport retries, legacy standalone RAG/chat and provider-side generation behavior are separate contracts",
    "authorize_run is opt-in for existing apps and does not replace tool policies, resource scopes or atomic business authorization",
    "The new product_lookup application is single-run and not a governed-source multi-turn history; hosts must use appropriately governed tools/source validators for that separate flow",
    "The new example uses a synthetic local ledger and structured fixture model, with no real shop authentication, natural-language quality or independent onboarding result",
    "Local POSIX/SQLite scope does not establish distributed recovery, production sandbox isolation or superiority to upstream frameworks"
  ],
